Korean School Records Toolkit Lite (korean-school-records-lite) — license notice

This is the documents-only edition of korean-school-records-toolkit (https://github.com/blueshadow62/korean-school-records-toolkit). It holds one skill, write-school-records, and its reference documents. It does not hold scripts or the korean-character-count skill.
- write-school-records: the source SKILL.md declares CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. © 2026 류기현(부산 동아공고). Non-commercial use only; derivatives must stay under the same license; attribution required. Commercial licensing inquiries via this repository's GitHub Issues.

This notice does not relicense third-party material. Copyright and license notices embedded in each skill remain controlling for that component.

The achievement-standards reference corpus under `skills/write-school-records/references/achievement-standards/` is derived from public Ministry of Education materials. Common/core-course materials follow the NCIC Korea Open Government License Type 2 terms, and elective-course materials follow the NKIS Korea Open Government License Type 1 terms. Its source-specific attribution and reuse information is recorded in that directory's `ATTRIBUTION.md` and `sources.json`; those notices must be retained with redistributed copies.

The middle-school achievement-standards reference corpus under `skills/write-school-records/references/achievement-standards-middle/` is derived from the 2022 revised curriculum achievement-standard materials posted on NCIC (https://ncic.re.kr). The NCIC copyright policy states Korea Open Government License Type 2 (attribution, non-commercial). The license marking of each posting was not checked one by one. Its attribution is recorded in that directory's `ATTRIBUTION.md` and `sources.json`; those notices must be retained with redistributed copies.

The Ministry of Education's school-record guidelines (2026, Korea Open Government License Type 4: attribution, non-commercial, no derivatives) are not included in this distribution. The files `skills/write-school-records/references/guidelines/summary.md` and `skills/write-school-records/references/guidelines-middle/summary.md` are summaries written for this skill from those guidelines; quoted directive articles are marked as quotations. The official text is available from the Ministry of Education website (https://www.moe.go.kr/boardCnts/viewRenew.do?boardID=316&lev=0&statusYN=W&s=moe&m=030215&opType=N&boardSeq=105372, posted 2026-02-19). Attribution and the status of these summaries are recorded in each directory's `ATTRIBUTION.md`.

The files `skills/write-school-records/references/holistic-evaluation.md` and `skills/write-school-records/references/major-*.md` were written for this skill from third-party documents: a joint study by five universities on common evaluation elements for comprehensive student-record admission, and department guides of Korea University. No reuse license was found for those documents. Their sources and the extent of reuse are recorded in `skills/write-school-records/references/source-policy.md`.
